# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
#
# .clang-tidy - static analysis policy (GODS_LAWS.md L-23 portao 3;
# FUND-4). Curated start, not the full check catalog turned on: a first
# pass with every group enabled drowns real findings in noise, and this
# is a young codebase where the signal-to-noise ratio of the ruleset
# matters more than maximal coverage on day one. Widen the enabled
# groups later as the codebase grows past the core layer, not now.
#
# NOLINT policy (mandatory, not mechanically enforced by clang-tidy
# itself): every NOLINT/NOLINTNEXTLINE in this tree MUST carry a
# `reason: ...` justification on the same line, e.g.
#   x = f(); // NOLINT(bugprone-foo) reason: <why this is not a bug here>
# tools/preci.sh's clang-tidy stage greps the same file list for
# NOLINT/NOLINTNEXTLINE and fails the build if one is missing the
# "reason:" marker - a suppression with no recorded reason is exactly
# the kind of finding a reviewer cannot audit later.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  performance-*,
  cert-*,
  misc-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-throwing-static-initialization,
  -cert-err58-cpp,
  -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-use-anonymous-namespace
# cert-err58-cpp and bugprone-throwing-static-initialization excluded
# together: both fire on the SAME static-init self-registration object
# that tests/harness/test_registry.hpp's GLINTFX_TEST macro expands to
# in every single test file (GODS_LAWS.md L-07 "no Catch2/GoogleTest"
# is exactly why that idiom exists here). Measured live building this
# slice: run-clang-tidy against the two-case tests/version_test.cpp
# alone produced one finding per check per case (2+2) before this
# exclusion - that is not two isolated bugs, it is the harness idiom
# repeating at every call site, forever, project-wide.
#
# misc-use-anonymous-namespace excluded for the same macro, same
# measurement: GLINTFX_TEST forward-declares its per-case function as
# `static void glintfx_test_fn_##name();` (test_registry.hpp) rather
# than inside the anonymous namespace the check wants, because the
# later out-of-namespace definition has to match that exact forward
# declaration. Moving it would mean redesigning the harness macro, not
# fixing a lint finding.
#
# misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes excluded: GODS_LAWS.md
# L-19 explicitly makes core value types (glintfx::version, and future
# vec2/rect) PUBLIC-layout on purpose ("value type do nucleo e visivel,
# e muda-lo e mudanca de ABI assumida") - the check's premise (public
# data members are an encapsulation smell) is the opposite of this
# project's own architectural decision for that category of type.
#
# misc-include-cleaner and bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
# excluded as pure noise-to-signal calls for a codebase this size: both
# fire on nearly every translation unit and every multi-parameter
# function respectively, with a false-positive rate that would train
# reviewers to stop reading clang-tidy output rather than sharpen it.
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '(include|src)/.*'
FormatStyle: none
